---
import ProductLayout from '@/layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import { PILLOWCASE_SPECS } from '@/data/specs';
import { pageTitle } from '@/lib/seo';
---

<ProductLayout
  title={pageTitle('Hotel Pillowcases')}
  description="Hotel pillowcases in cotton, mercerized satin and jacquard, 58 × 85 cm, cut to match the sheet line. Wholesale."
  h1="Hotel pillowcases"
  breadcrumb="Pillowcases"
  specs={PILLOWCASE_SPECS}
  images={['products-pillowcases-hero', 'products-pillowcases-detail']}
>
  <p>
    Pillowcases are 58 × 85 cm and cut from the same cloth as the sheets they ship with. Ordering
    them together is the only way to guarantee the whites match after a year of laundering, since
    dye lots drift even in the same construction.
  </p>
  <p>
    Plain cotton for standard rooms, mercerized satin for suites, jacquard where the bedding
    pattern has to run through the pillow. The housekeeping that replaces pillowcases most often
    is usually the plain one.
  </p>
  <p>
    Housekeeping style matters here too: envelope closure or open end. Tell us which the property
    uses and we will cut to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloth, thread counts and supply terms are on the
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href="/hotel-bedding-supplier/">hotel bedding supplier</a>
    page; the sheet and duvet range is on
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href="/hotel-linens/">hotel linens</a>.
  </p>
</ProductLayout>
